    "chunk_text": "\u0d85\u0dc0\u0db0\u0dcf\u0db1\u0d9c\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca \u0db4\u0dc3\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db1 \u0d9c\u0dbd\u0dc3 \u0db0\u0dd3\u0dc0\u0dbb \u0dc3\u0dd9 \u0db1\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0d9a \u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0d9c\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dca \u0d89\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0dc3\u0dd2\u0da7\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dd4 \u0dbd\u0dd0\u0d9c\u0dda.\n\nwww.meteo.gov.lk\n\nhttps://was.meteo.gov.lk\n\n\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dcf\u0da5: S. Jayasekara\n\n0112686686\n\n\u0db4\u0dd4\u0daf\u0dbb\u0ddd\u0d9a\u0dae\u0db1\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1 \u0dbd\u0daf \u0dc3\u0dca\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1 \u0dc3\u0dc4 \u0dad\u0dd3\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dcf:\n\n\u0daf\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dba \u0daf\u0dda\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc0 \u0dc3\u0dca\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dba (\u0d8b\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dca\u0dcf\u0d82\u0dc1/ \u0db1\u0dd0\u0daf\u0d9c\u0db1\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dbb \u0daf\u0dda\u0dc1\u0dcf\u0d82\u0dc1)\n\n\u0d9a\u0dd0\u0dc5\u0db9\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dd2 \u0dc3\u0dca\u0dc0\u0db7\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dba\n\nwww.meteo.gov.lk\n\nhttps://was.meteo.gov.lk\n\nDuty Meteorologist: S. Jayasekara\n\n0112686686\n\nSTRONG WINDS AND ROUGH SEAS\n\nDepartment of Meteorology Natural Hazards Early Warning Centre\n\nIssued at 14 November 2026\n\n05:00 pm\n\nValid From 14 November 2026\n\n05:30 pm\n\nValid Until 16 November 2026\n\n05:30 pm\n\nBulletin No MSA/26/11/14/01-\n\nEN\n\nFor Multi-day boats in the Southeast Bay of Bengal deep sea areas and the sea areas off the coast extending from Kankasanthurai to Hambantota via Trincomalee and Pottuvil.\n\nThe low-pressure area located in the Bay of Bengal, east of Sri Lanka, was located approximately 650 km east\n\nof Batticaloa. The system is expected to move northwestwards, away from the eastern coast of the island\n\nand likely to intensify into a 'depression' by tomorrow (November 15). Thereafter, it is likely to move north-\n\nnorthwestwards and intensify further into a cyclonic storm over the south and adjoining west-central Bay\n\nof Bengal around 16th November.\n\nTherefore, Naval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to the deep-sea areas bounded\n\nby 05N-15N and 80E-90E, and the sea areas off the coast extending from Kankasanthurai to\n\nHambanthota via Trincomalee and Pottuvil, from 5.30am on 14 November 2026 until further notice.\n\nFurther, Naval and fishing communities operating in those sea areas are advised to move to safe\n\nareas.\n\nThe naval and fishing communities, are requested to be attentive to the future forecasts and bulletins issued\n\nby the Department of Meteorology in this regard.\n\nwww.meteo.gov.lk\n\nhttps://was.meteo.gov.lk\n\nDuty Meteorologist: S. Jayasekara\n\n0112686686\n\nForecast location and intensity: Date Time Location (Lat 0N/ Long 0E)\n\nCategory of cyclonic disturbance"
