    "chunk_text": "\u0d85\u0dc0\u0db0\u0dcf\u0db1\u0daf\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca \u0db4\u0dc3\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0db1 \u0daf\u0dbd\u0dc3 \u0db0\u0dd3\u0dc0\u0dbb \u0dc3\u0dc4 \u0db1\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0d9a \u0db4\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0daf\u0d9c\u0db1\u0dca \u0d89\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0dc3\u0dd2\u0da7\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dd4 \u0dbd\u0dd0\u0daf\u0dda.\n\nwww.meteo.gov.lk\n\nhttps://was.meteo.gov.lk\n\n\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dcf\u0da5: S. Wikramasuriya\n\n0112686686\n\n\u0db4\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dbb\u0ddd\u0d9a\u0dae\u0db1\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0db1 \u0dbd\u0daf \u0dc3\u0dca\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1 \u0dc3\u0dc4 \u0dad\u0dd3\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dcf:\n\n\u0daf\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dba \u0db8\u0dda\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc0 \u0dc3\u0dca\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dba (\u0d8b\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dca\u0dcf\u0d82\u0dc1/ \u0db1\u0dd0\u0db8\u0d9c\u0db1\u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dda\u0dc1\u0dcf\u0d82\u0dc1)\n\n\u0d9a\u0dd0\u0dc5\u0db9\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dd2 \u0dc3\u0dca\u0dc0\u0db7\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dba\n\nwww.meteo.gov.lk\n\nhttps://was.meteo.gov.lk\n\n\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dcf\u0da5: S. Wikramasuriya\n\n0112686686\n\nSource: https://rsmcnewdelhi.imd.gov.in\n\nwww.meteo.gov.lk\n\nhttps://was.meteo.gov.lk\n\nDuty Meteorologist: S. Wikramasuriya\n\n0112686686\n\nWARNING FOR STRONG WINDS AND ROUGH SEAS\n\nDepartment of Meteorology Natural Hazards Early Warning Centre\n\nIssued at 16 November 2026\n\n07:00 AM\n\nValid From 16 November 2026\n\n07:00 AM\n\nValid Until 17 November 2026\n\n07:00 AM\n\nBulletin No MSW/26/11/16/01-EN\n\nFor Multi-day boats in the West-Central Bay of Bengal deep sea areas and the sea areas off the coast extending from Kankasanthurai to Hambantota via Trincomalee and Pottuvil.\n\nThe low-pressure area located to the East of Sri Lanka, in the Bay of Bengal, has developed into a \u2018Depression.\u2019\n\nAs of 5:30 a.m. today, this system was positioned approximately 600 km northeast of Trincomalee. It is highly\n\nlikely that the system will continue to move in a north-westwards, staying well off the east coast of Sri Lanka\u2014\n\nand intensify into a \u2018Deep Depression\u2019 by tomorrow morning (November 16). By tomorrow night, it is expected\n\nto develop into a \u2018Cyclonic Storm\u2019 over the southern and adjacent west-central Bay of Bengal, and further\n\nintensify into a \u2018Severe Cyclonic Storm\u2019 over the west-central Bay of Bengal by November 17.\n\nTherefore, Naval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to the deep-sea areas bounded\n\nby 05N-15N and 80E-90E, and the sea areas off the coast extending from Kankasanthurai to\n\nHambanthota via Trincomalee and Pottuvil, until further notice. Further, Naval and fishing\n\ncommunities operating in those sea areas are advised to move to safe areas.\n\nThe naval and fishing communities, are requested to be attentive to the future forecasts and bulletins issued"
