    "chunk_text": "For Multi-day boats in the West-Central Bay of Bengal deep sea areas and the sea areas off the coast extending from Kankasanthurai to Pottuvil via Trincomalee and Batticaloa.\n\nThe Deep Depression over the Southeast Bay of Bengal and adjoining Southwest Bay of Bengal has intensified into a Cyclonic Storm and has been named \u201cAkvan\u201d (pronounced: Akvan).\n\n2026.The system is very likely to continue moving north-northwestwards and intensify further into a Severe\n\nCyclonic Storm over the Westcentral Bay of Bengal around 05.30 p.m. on 17th November 2026.\n\nThereafter, it is likely to move northwestwards and further intensify into a Very Severe Cyclonic Storm around\n\n05.30 a.m. on 19th November 2026.Continuing its northwestward movement, the system is likely to cross the\n\nAndhra Pradesh and Yanam coasts between Nellore and Tuni around 11.30 a.m. on 20th November 2026 as a\n\nVery Severe Cyclonic Storm.\n\nTherefore, Naval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to the deep-sea areas bounded by\n\n05N-17N and 80E-90E, and the sea areas off the coast extending from Kankasanthurai to Pottuvil via\n\nTrincomalee and Batticaloa, until further notice. Further, Naval and fishing communities operating in\n\nthose sea areas are advised to move to safe areas.\n\nThe naval and fishing communities, are requested to be attentive to the future forecasts and bulletins issued by\n\nthe Department of Meteorology in this regard.\n\nwww.meteo.gov.lk\n\nhttps://was.meteo.gov.lk\n\nDuty Meteorologist: Udeni Weerasinghe\n\n0112686686\n\nForecast location and intensity:\n\nDate Time Location (Lat 0N/ Long 0E)\n\nCategory of cyclonic disturbance"
