    "chunk_text": "Bulletin No MSW/26/11/17/01-\n\nEN\n\nFor Multi-day boats in the West-Central Bay of Bengal deep sea areas and the sea areas off the coast extending from Kankasanthurai to Pottuvil via Trincomalee and Batticaloa.\n\nThe system is very likely to continue move slowly north-northwestwards and intensify further into a Severe Cyclonic Storm over the Westcentral Bay of Bengal around 05.30 a.m. on 18 th November 2026. Thereafter, it is likely to move northwestwards and intensify further into a very severe cyclonic storm around 05.30 p.m. of 19th November, 2026.\n\nContinuing to move northwestward, it is likely to cross Andhra Pradesh & Yanam coasts between Nellore and Visakhapatnam, around 11.30 a.m. of 20th November, 2026 as a Very severe cyclonic storm.\n\nTherefore, Naval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to the deep-sea areas bounded by 06N-19N and 80E-95E, and the sea areas off the coast extending from Kankasanthurai to Pottuvil via Trincomalee and Batticaloa, until further notice. Further, Naval and fishing communities operating in those sea areas are advised to move to safe areas.\n\nThe naval and fishing communities, are requested to be attentive to the future forecasts and bulletins issued by the Department of Meteorology in this regard.\n\nwww.meteo.gov.lk\n\nhttps://was.meteo.gov.lk\n\nDuty Meteorologist: Maneesha Wijesinghe\n\n0112686686\n\nForecast location and intensity:\n\nDate Time Location (Lat 0N/ Long 0E)\n\nCategory of cyclonic disturbance"
