Centre\n\nIssued at 18 November 2026\n\n10:00 am\n\nValid From 18 November 2026\n\n10:00 am\n\nValid Until 19 November 2026\n\n10:00 am\n\nBulletin No MSW/26/11/18/01-\n\nEN\n\nFor Multi-day boats in the West-Central Bay of Bengal deep sea areas and the sea areas off the coast extending from Kankasanthurai to Pottuvil via Trincomalee and Batticaloa.\n\nThe Cyclone \u201cAkvan\u201d over South and adjoining West-central Bay of Bengal was intensified into a severe cyclonic storm and lay centered, near Latitude 12.7\u00b0N and Longitude 85.5\u00b0E (approximately 650 km from Trincomalee) at around 05.30 a.m. today (18th November 2026).\n\nContinuing to move north-northwestward, it is likely to cross Andhra Pradesh coasts between Nellore and Visakhapatnam, India around 11.30 am of 20th November.\n\nTherefore, Naval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to the deep-sea areas bounded by 06N-20N and 80E-95E, and the sea areas off the coast extending from Kankasanthurai to Pottuvil via Trincomalee and Batticaloa, until further notice. Further, Naval and fishing communities operating in those sea areas are advised to move to safe areas.\n\nThe naval and fishing communities, are requested to be attentive to the future forecasts and bulletins issued by the Department of Meteorology in this regard.\n\nwww.meteo.gov.lk\n\nhttps://was.meteo.gov.lk\n\nDuty Meteorologist: S.Jayasekara\n\n0112686686"
