Centre\n\nIssued at 18 November 2026\n\n03:00 pm\n\nValid From 18 November 2026\n\n03:00 pm\n\nValid Until 19 November 2026\n\n03:00 pm\n\nBulletin No MSW/26/11/18/02-\n\nEN\n\nFor Multi-day boats in the West-Central Bay of Bengal deep sea areas.\n\nThe Severe Cyclonic storm \u201cAkvan\u201d over South and adjoining West-central Bay of Bengal, lay centered, near Latitude 13.1\u00b0N and Longitude 85.4\u00b0E (approximately 680 km northeast to Trincomalee) at around 11.30 a.m. today (18th November 2026).\n\nContinuing to move north-northwestward, it is likely to cross Andhra Pradesh coasts between Nellore and Visakhapatnam, India around 11.30 am of 20th November.\n\nTherefore, Naval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to the deep-sea areas bounded by 10N-20N and 80E-95E, until further notice. Further, Naval and fishing communities operating in those sea areas are advised to move to safe areas.\n\nThe naval and fishing communities, are requested to be attentive to the future forecasts and bulletins issued by the Department of Meteorology in this regard.\n\nwww.meteo.gov.lk\n\nhttps://was.meteo.gov.lk\n\nDuty Meteorologist: S.Jayasekara\n\n0112686686\n\nForecast location and intensity:\n\nDate Time Location (Lat 0N/ Long 0E)\n\nCategory of cyclonic disturbance"
