e\n\nIssued at 19 November 2026\n\n04:00 pm\n\nValid From 19 November 2026\n\n04:00 pm\n\nValid Until 20 November 2026\n\n04:00 pm\n\nBulletin No MSW/26/11/19/01-EN\n\nFor Multi-day boats in the West-Central Bay of Bengal deep sea areas.\n\nThe Severe Cyclonic Storm \u201cAkvan\u201d over the west-central Bay of Bengal moved northwards with the speed of 17 kmph during past 06 hours and lay centered, near Latitude 15.4\u00b0N and Longitude 85.2\u00b0E (approximately 830 km northeast to Kankesanthurai) at around 11.30 a.m. today (19th November 2026).\n\nContinuing to move north-northwestward, it is likely to cross Andhra Pradesh coasts between Narsapur and Puri, India around 11.30 am of 20th November.\n\nTherefore, Naval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to the deep-sea areas bounded by 12N-20N and 80E-93E, until further notice. Further, Naval and fishing communities operating in those sea areas are advised to move to safe areas.\n\nThe naval and fishing communities, are requested to be attentive to the future forecasts and bulletins issued by the Department of Meteorology in this regard.\n\nwww.meteo.gov.lk\n\nhttps://was.meteo.gov.lk\n\nDuty Meteorologist: A.I.Randika\n\n0112686686\n\nForecast location and intensity:\n\nDate Time Location (Lat 0N/ Long 0E)\n\nCategory of cyclonic disturbance"
